<title>USA: Family Bargain CEO Mowbray resigns.</title>
<headline>Family Bargain CEO Mowbray resigns.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Family Bargain Corp announced Friday that William Mowbray had resigned as president, chief executive officer and a member of the board of directors.</p>
<p>In a statement,  Family Bargain, operator of 162 off-price retail stores, said it had hired Herbert Mines &amp; Associates of New York to conduct a search for a successor to Mowbray. In the interim, senior management will report to Chairman James Somerville.</p>
</text>
